1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,599
Last lesson Gradle tested your code. Today it manages everything your code needs.

2
00:00:06,149 --> 00:00:06,731
Libraries,

3
00:00:06,731 --> 00:00:07,953
where they come from,

4
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:10,282
and the plug ins that add new abilities.

5
00:00:10,282 --> 00:00:12,378
All of it lives in one build script.

6
00:00:12,928 --> 00:00:17,591
A wrong choice here has a price: a test library shipped inside your app,

7
00:00:17,591 --> 00:00:20,247
version numbers scattered over ten files,

8
00:00:20,247 --> 00:00:21,931
a jar nobody can download.

9
00:00:22,481 --> 00:00:26,584
You will fix all three on a real project: the scope of a library,

10
00:00:26,584 --> 00:00:27,720
a version catalog,

11
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:28,667
and publishing.

12
00:00:29,217 --> 00:00:32,332
Then you do it alone, and a checker judges your result.

13
00:00:32,882 --> 00:00:36,957
One idea first: a build script says what you need, and where to get it.

14
00:00:38,507 --> 00:00:41,707
Four ideas run every Gradle dependency setup.

15
00:00:42,257 --> 00:00:42,537
One,

16
00:00:42,537 --> 00:00:43,448
repositories.

17
00:00:43,448 --> 00:00:45,409
They say where Gradle looks.

18
00:00:45,409 --> 00:00:47,791
Maven central is the public store,

19
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:49,892
and a company can add its own,

20
00:00:49,892 --> 00:00:50,662
like Nexus.

21
00:00:51,212 --> 00:00:51,483
Two,

22
00:00:51,483 --> 00:00:51,957
scopes.

23
00:00:51,957 --> 00:00:54,597
Implementation ships with your program.

24
00:00:54,597 --> 00:00:57,169
Test implementation is only for tests,

25
00:00:57,169 --> 00:00:58,252
and never ships.

26
00:00:58,802 --> 00:00:59,239
Three,

27
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:00,693
the version catalog.

28
00:01:00,693 --> 00:01:01,347
One file,

29
00:01:01,347 --> 00:01:03,383
libs dot versions dot tom L,

30
00:01:03,383 --> 00:01:05,928
holds every name and every version.

31
00:01:06,478 --> 00:01:06,843
Four,

32
00:01:06,843 --> 00:01:07,499
plug ins.

33
00:01:07,499 --> 00:01:10,345
The java plug in adds compile and test.

34
00:01:10,345 --> 00:01:14,286
The maven publish plug in adds one more task: publish.

35
00:01:14,836 --> 00:01:20,254
Maven does the same jobs in a pom. Gradle does them in a script. Let us see it live.

36
00:01:22,304 --> 00:01:28,320
Go into the project. Type: CD, slash opt, slash lab ninety-seven, slash cartcore.

37
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:29,296
First,

38
00:01:29,296 --> 00:01:31,354
where do libraries come from?

39
00:01:31,354 --> 00:01:33,340
Show the repositories block.

40
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,121
Type: grep,

41
00:01:34,121 --> 00:01:35,469
dash capital A two,

42
00:01:35,469 --> 00:01:35,895
quote,

43
00:01:35,895 --> 00:01:36,321
caret,

44
00:01:36,321 --> 00:01:37,243
repositories,

45
00:01:37,243 --> 00:01:37,669
quote,

46
00:01:37,669 --> 00:01:38,875
build dot gradle.

47
00:01:40,925 --> 00:01:41,897
Maven central.

48
00:01:41,897 --> 00:01:43,633
The public library store,

49
00:01:43,633 --> 00:01:45,299
the same one Maven uses.

50
00:01:45,299 --> 00:01:46,618
Gradle searches it,

51
00:01:46,618 --> 00:01:48,770
and downloads what you ask for,

52
00:01:48,770 --> 00:01:49,117
once.

53
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:51,111
Now what we ask for.

54
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:51,905
Type: grep,

55
00:01:51,905 --> 00:01:53,349
dash capital A five,

56
00:01:53,349 --> 00:01:53,782
quote,

57
00:01:53,782 --> 00:01:54,215
caret,

58
00:01:54,215 --> 00:01:55,154
dependencies,

59
00:01:55,154 --> 00:01:55,587
quote,

60
00:01:55,587 --> 00:01:56,814
build dot gradle.

61
00:01:58,864 --> 00:02:01,419
Look at the third implementation line.

62
00:02:01,419 --> 00:02:01,890
J unit,

63
00:02:01,890 --> 00:02:02,898
a test library,

64
00:02:02,898 --> 00:02:04,915
is declared as implementation.

65
00:02:04,915 --> 00:02:07,403
That means it ships with the program.

66
00:02:07,403 --> 00:02:08,613
That is a mistake.

67
00:02:09,163 --> 00:02:10,353
Let us prove it.

68
00:02:10,353 --> 00:02:13,996
Count the J unit lines on the runtime class path.

69
00:02:13,996 --> 00:02:15,855
Type: dot slash gradle W,

70
00:02:15,855 --> 00:02:16,821
dependencies,

71
00:02:16,821 --> 00:02:18,606
dash dash configuration,

72
00:02:18,606 --> 00:02:20,019
runtime class path,

73
00:02:20,019 --> 00:02:20,762
then grep,

74
00:02:20,762 --> 00:02:21,283
dash C,

75
00:02:21,283 --> 00:02:21,729
junit.

76
00:02:24,279 --> 00:02:25,242
More than zero.

77
00:02:25,242 --> 00:02:27,553
J unit is on the runtime class path.

78
00:02:27,553 --> 00:02:30,892
Your app would carry a test framework to production.

79
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:33,032
Fix the scope with sed.

80
00:02:33,032 --> 00:02:38,077
Only the J unit line changes: implementation becomes test implementation.

81
00:02:40,127 --> 00:02:41,812
Count again. Same command.

82
00:02:48,962 --> 00:02:49,279
Zero.

83
00:02:49,279 --> 00:02:52,004
J unit is gone from the runtime class path.

84
00:02:52,004 --> 00:02:54,032
It is still there for the tests,

85
00:02:54,032 --> 00:02:55,490
but it no longer ships.

86
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,231
Now the versions.

87
00:02:57,231 --> 00:03:01,014
Numbers scattered through a script are hard to change.

88
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,886
A version catalog keeps them in one file.

89
00:03:03,886 --> 00:03:04,586
Create it.

90
00:03:04,586 --> 00:03:05,567
Type: print F,

91
00:03:05,567 --> 00:03:06,898
the versions table,

92
00:03:06,898 --> 00:03:07,738
into gradle,

93
00:03:07,738 --> 00:03:10,120
slash libs dot versions dot tom L.

94
00:03:12,170 --> 00:03:13,924
Add the library: its module,

95
00:03:13,924 --> 00:03:15,866
and a reference to the version.

96
00:03:15,866 --> 00:03:16,492
Same file,

97
00:03:16,492 --> 00:03:18,058
with double greater than.

98
00:03:25,108 --> 00:03:30,143
Read the file. Type: cat, gradle, slash libs dot versions dot tom L.

99
00:03:32,193 --> 00:03:32,931
Two tables.

100
00:03:32,931 --> 00:03:34,744
Versions holds the numbers.

101
00:03:34,744 --> 00:03:36,490
Libraries holds the names,

102
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:38,974
and points to a version by reference.

103
00:03:38,974 --> 00:03:40,518
Change one number here,

104
00:03:40,518 --> 00:03:43,137
and every project that uses it follows.

105
00:03:43,687 --> 00:03:48,721
Use it in the build script. Replace the long text with libs dot commons dot text.

106
00:03:52,071 --> 00:03:57,063
Look at the commons lines. Type: grep dash N, commons, build dot gradle.

107
00:03:59,113 --> 00:04:00,798
Libs dot commons dot text.

108
00:04:00,798 --> 00:04:02,030
Short and readable,

109
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:04,428
and the version lives in the catalog.

110
00:04:04,428 --> 00:04:07,344
Commons lang three still has its number here.

111
00:04:07,344 --> 00:04:09,353
Moving it is part of your task.

112
00:04:09,903 --> 00:04:13,082
Does it still build? Run the tests. Keep the build line.

113
00:04:15,632 --> 00:04:19,024
Build successful. Same library, same version, new home.

114
00:04:19,574 --> 00:04:23,350
Plug ins now. Add the maven publish plug in, next to java.

115
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,565
Check the plug ins block.

116
00:04:28,565 --> 00:04:30,825
Type: grep dash capital A three,

117
00:04:30,825 --> 00:04:31,249
quote,

118
00:04:31,249 --> 00:04:31,672
caret,

119
00:04:31,672 --> 00:04:32,237
plugins,

120
00:04:32,237 --> 00:04:32,661
quote,

121
00:04:32,661 --> 00:04:33,861
build dot gradle.

122
00:04:35,911 --> 00:04:42,205
Two plug ins. Java builds and tests. Maven publish can send the result to a repository.

123
00:04:42,755 --> 00:04:44,317
Describe what to publish.

124
00:04:44,317 --> 00:04:45,316
One publication,

125
00:04:45,316 --> 00:04:47,190
built from the java component.

126
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:48,877
Add it to the build script.

127
00:04:53,327 --> 00:04:54,847
And where to publish it.

128
00:04:54,847 --> 00:04:55,671
A repository,

129
00:04:55,671 --> 00:04:56,938
in the build folder.

130
00:04:56,938 --> 00:04:59,471
In real life this address is your Nexus.

131
00:05:02,921 --> 00:05:07,252
Publish. Type: dot slash gradle W, publish, and grep, build.

132
00:05:10,302 --> 00:05:13,907
Build successful. The new task, publish, came from the plug in.

133
00:05:14,457 --> 00:05:18,127
What was published? Find the cart core files, and hide the checksums.

134
00:05:21,077 --> 00:05:21,508
A jar,

135
00:05:21,508 --> 00:05:21,939
a pom,

136
00:05:21,939 --> 00:05:23,736
and a Gradle module file.

137
00:05:23,736 --> 00:05:27,690
This is exactly what Nexus would store for other teams.

138
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:34,832
Read the pom. List its artifact I Ds. Type: grep, artifact I D, and the path to the pom.

139
00:05:36,882 --> 00:05:37,570
Cart core,

140
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:38,465
commons text,

141
00:05:38,465 --> 00:05:40,048
and commons lang three.

142
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:42,663
No J unit: a test library never ships.

143
00:05:42,663 --> 00:05:43,833
Your two choices,

144
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:45,623
the scope and the catalog,

145
00:05:45,623 --> 00:05:48,445
show up in the file other teams download.

146
00:05:49,995 --> 00:05:53,515
Your task. The same journey, on your own project, in the lab.

147
00:05:54,065 --> 00:05:56,904
One: J unit is declared as implementation.

148
00:05:56,904 --> 00:05:58,661
Make it a test dependency,

149
00:05:58,661 --> 00:06:01,297
and prove it on the runtime class path.

150
00:06:01,847 --> 00:06:06,143
Two: create a version catalog for commons text and J unit jupiter,

151
00:06:06,143 --> 00:06:07,771
and use it in the script.

152
00:06:07,771 --> 00:06:09,463
The tests must still pass.

153
00:06:10,013 --> 00:06:14,685
Three: add the maven publish plug in and the publishing block, and run publish.

154
00:06:15,235 --> 00:06:19,118
Four: read the pom. It lists commons text, and no J unit.

155
00:06:19,668 --> 00:06:24,148
Five: write notes dot text, three lines: catalog, published, and scope.

156
00:06:26,198 --> 00:06:30,401
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

157
00:06:30,951 --> 00:06:32,650
The lab lives on git hub,

158
00:06:32,650 --> 00:06:33,805
at it dash waves,

159
00:06:33,805 --> 00:06:35,368
slash dev ops dash A I,

160
00:06:35,368 --> 00:06:36,863
in the folder academy,

161
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:37,543
slash lab.

162
00:06:38,093 --> 00:06:43,426
Two files: lab ninety-seven dot S H, and shortcuts ninety-seven dot S H.

163
00:06:43,976 --> 00:06:44,846
Install it,

164
00:06:44,846 --> 00:06:48,404
in your Ubuntu virtual machine: sudo install,

165
00:06:48,404 --> 00:06:50,222
dash m seven five five,

166
00:06:50,222 --> 00:06:52,199
lab ninety-seven dot S H,

167
00:06:52,199 --> 00:06:53,385
into slash usr,

168
00:06:53,385 --> 00:06:54,334
slash local,

169
00:06:54,334 --> 00:06:55,283
slash S bin.

170
00:06:55,833 --> 00:07:00,122
Load the short name with: source shortcuts ninety-seven dot S H.

171
00:07:00,122 --> 00:07:01,865
Then you can type: lab up,

172
00:07:01,865 --> 00:07:02,535
lab check,

173
00:07:02,535 --> 00:07:03,406
and lab down.

174
00:07:03,956 --> 00:07:05,128
You need a J D K,

175
00:07:05,128 --> 00:07:06,644
curl and python three,

176
00:07:06,644 --> 00:07:08,644
about one gigabyte of memory,

177
00:07:08,644 --> 00:07:10,505
and an internet connection.

178
00:07:10,505 --> 00:07:12,849
The first lab up downloads Gradle,

179
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,089
and the libraries.

180
00:07:14,639 --> 00:07:18,927
Lab down removes everything. Only run it in your own virtual machine.

181
00:07:20,977 --> 00:07:23,046
Pass or fail. You need all six.

182
00:07:23,596 --> 00:07:25,410
Five pass lines in lab check.

183
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:29,373
J unit is test only: not on the runtime class path.

184
00:07:29,923 --> 00:07:33,059
The versions live in the catalog, and the tests still pass.

185
00:07:33,609 --> 00:07:36,702
Maven publish is applied, and publish really ran.

186
00:07:37,252 --> 00:07:40,516
Notes dot text names the real files, in your own words.

187
00:07:41,066 --> 00:07:42,922
Lab down leaves nothing behind.

188
00:07:43,472 --> 00:07:44,774
To pass, all six.

189
00:07:46,824 --> 00:07:49,661
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

190
00:07:50,211 --> 00:07:52,302
One: lab up, and read the task file.

191
00:07:52,852 --> 00:07:55,497
Two: change the scope of J unit, and prove it.

192
00:07:56,047 --> 00:07:58,501
Three: write the version catalog, and use it.

193
00:07:59,051 --> 00:08:02,613
Four: add the plug in, the publishing block, and run publish.

194
00:08:03,163 --> 00:08:06,342
Five: read the pom, write the notes, and run lab check.

195
00:08:06,892 --> 00:08:09,473
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

196
00:08:10,023 --> 00:08:11,858
Pause the video, and begin now.

197
00:08:27,408 --> 00:08:28,283
Quick check.

198
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:32,737
What is the difference between implementation and test implementation?

199
00:08:33,287 --> 00:08:35,143
What does a version catalog give you?

200
00:08:35,693 --> 00:08:39,661
Which plug in adds the publish task, and where did your jar and pom go?

201
00:08:40,211 --> 00:08:42,472
Why is J unit missing from the pom?

202
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:45,297
Objective covered: M C eleven,

203
00:08:45,297 --> 00:08:46,510
objective three,

204
00:08:46,510 --> 00:08:48,027
Gradle dependencies,

205
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,998
repositories and plug ins.

206
00:08:50,548 --> 00:08:52,617
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

207
